nc -vz is actually the quickest for just checking if the port is open/reachable — it doesn't care about the protocol. curl is better when you want to validate the actual HTTP response from your app.

network troubleshooting flow from outside in:
Host network
    └── Docker bridge network
            └── catalogue container (port open?)
                    └── mongodb container (reachable from app?)
Each step confirms one more layer is working — port open → app responding → routes exist → dependencies connected.

