REMIANING DEBUGGUNG
Here's a complete troubleshooting checklist for this setup:
Network
bashdocker network inspect bridge          # all containers, IPs, same network?
docker inspect catalogue | grep -i ip  # correct IP?
Container health
bashdocker ps                              # running? restart count?
docker stats                           # CPU/memory usage normal?
docker logs catalogue                  # any errors/exceptions?
docker logs mongodb                    # mongo startup errors?
App behavior
bash# does the app return correct data?
wget -qO- http://catalogue:8080/catalogue

# response time ok?
curl -w "%{time_total}" http://localhost:80/health
MongoDB
bash# can you query mongo directly?
docker exec -it mongodb mongo
> show dbs
> use catalogue
> show collections
Resources
bashdocker stats --no-stream   # is any container eating too much CPU/RAM?
df -h                      # disk space ok on host?
Logs
bashdocker logs --tail 50 catalogue        # last 50 lines
docker logs --follow catalogue         # live logs
docker logs --since 5m catalogue       # last 5 minutes

The most important ones day-to-day are honestly just:

docker logs — catches 80% of issues
docker stats — catches resource problems
/health endpoint — confirms end to end in one shot